{"id":"04253b71-d143-45f1-bd11-b17e1b75bf65","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The Java main method always receives a non-null array for args, even if it is empty, according to the Java specification.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.028044Z"}
{"id":"6bddd666-b995-4c59-af52-89a557cee2fc","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The Java runtime guarantees that the parameter 'args' to main is never null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.028856Z"}
{"id":"3f43bb8a-27a3-45d0-b740-7c841683f4a0","expr":"b == 0 || (a / b) * b + (a % b) == a","rationale":"If b is not zero, integer division and modulus reconstruct a, otherwise division not evaluated.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.029521Z"}
{"id":"086f8202-bbfa-4466-be69-8cd87ddb8553","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Arrays in Java always have a non-negative length, including zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.028856Z"}
{"id":"0ef76b22-f58b-40d5-bd01-0c8f85b9f628","expr":"b == 0 || b > Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"For all nonzero b, b may not be Integer.MIN_VALUE if special handling is required for edge-case division.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.029521Z"}
{"id":"762b2ed5-4aca-485e-9180-e95e606981a2","expr":"args.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"The 'args' parameter is always an array at this method point.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.028856Z"}
{"id":"dddc822a-a5d7-4ddf-b5ac-0fc931ab7a58","expr":"b == 0 || a / b <= a","rationale":"For positive b, integer division result is less than or equal to a; safe because b == 0 is guarded.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.029521Z"}
{"id":"dfbb131d-b425-4c7e-8e6c-5b5190db2c7e","expr":"(b == 0) == (result == Integer.MIN_VALUE)","rationale":"If b==0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE; otherwise, it returns the division result.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.030444Z"}
{"id":"ee3737a8-56f7-4633-bace-2b87d5d19dba","expr":"(b != 0) == (result == a / b)","rationale":"If b is not zero, the method returns the integer division of a by b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.030444Z"}
{"id":"94964d63-6c66-4c40-a451-0b94fb74f29c","expr":"(b == 0) || (result == a / b)","rationale":"If b==0, result need not equal a/b, but if not, it must be a/b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.030444Z"}
{"id":"6e1769fc-49d4-480f-aba8-43083078de24","expr":"(b != 0) || (result == Integer.MIN_VALUE)","rationale":"If b==0, result is Integer.MIN_VALUE; otherwise, this is vacuously true.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-17T15:24:39.030444Z"}
